        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-15T10:37:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you explain why not? As far as I can tell the code does:\n\n    DynamicConfigDeviceSide dynamicConfig \u003d new DynamicConfigDeviceSide(\n        \"CtsNetTestCasesLatestSdk\");\n    sIpAddressEchoUrl \u003d dynamicConfig.getValue(\"IP_ADDRESS_ECHO_URL\");\n\nand if I\u0027m reading that correctly, that means it will load /sdcard/dynamic-config-files/CtsNetTestCasesLatestSdk.dynamic either via a contentprovider (using \"content://android.tradefed.contentprovider/sdcard/dynamic-config-files/CtsNetTestCasesLatestSdk.dynamic\") or via direct read.\n\nIt will parse that using an XML parser, it will will look for an \u003centry key\u003d\"IP_ADDRESS_ECHO_URL\"\u003e and if it finds it, it will load the value into sIpAddressEchoUrl.",
      "parentUuid": "69bf335e_0a326af2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 334,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 334,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "bafd34a66551444c7efff43089f65605485ec95f",
